{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213907,"nonce":"uvoFiFybKoCGjbHDYL1y953Ty/o=","title":"wasm: shadow stack for JIT'd locals, Immix heap in linear memory, fibers for JIT'd bodies","message":"Three pieces, in order.\n\n1. Shadow stack (fixes the open wasm GC-root issue). Emitted wasm keeps every MIR Value in an i64 local the collector cannot see. Give each JIT'd function a frame in a linear-memory shadow stack: on entry bump a shadow sp, store Values that live across calls into the frame, restore on exit; register the shadow region as a root range. Also root current_closure_cell, last_module_vars_cache, main_module_cache, parked_fibers, and write frame.values before tier::dispatch in dispatch_closure_bc_inner. Ash's equivalent is LLVM pinning pointer registers to its shadow stack (target_abi pointer_registers_in_memory); the cost is a store per live Value per call, not per instruction.\n2. Immix heap on wasm32: alloc_zeroed reservation aligned to the block size, no hand-back, word stride 4, default size configurable (today's nursery is 64 MiB per VM). Conservative scanning of Rust-in-wasm frames is not available (locals are not in linear memory), so the interpreter and helper roots stay precise on this target.\n3. Fibers for JIT'd wasm bodies. Ash suspends compiled wasm with a link-time unwind/rewind transform seeded from one host import (env.ash_host_fiber_yield) and driven through three exported globals; the host picks the mechanism (wasmtime async, JSPI, or the transform). wren_lift emits its own wasm from MIR and already has a state-machine transform for yielding functions, so apply that transform to yielding MIR before wasm emission instead of rewriting bytes after the fact. Route the actual suspension through a single import so the browser host can use JSPI where available and the worker/Promise bridge elsewhere. Functions that call yield then tier up instead of staying interpreted.\n\nBuild the wasm artifacts in CI, run the wasm arm of the test corpus under wasmtime (not a browser), keep the fibers-on arm last and diff its failure set against fibers-off so \"both green\" cannot hide a divergence.","files":null}]}